Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?lint(P11):=20require=20loading=20and=20decoding?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20on=20every=20JSX=20<img>=20=E2=80=94=20red=20on=20purpose?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 5 prep for P11, delivered fail-first. No component is changed: this adds
the rule, wires it, and adds its spec. Against origin/staging it reports 119
violations across 87 of the 158 JSX <img> tags the 0-D2-03 inventory counted,
in 53 files — 35 tags carry neither attribute, 84 carry loading but not
decoding. 71 tags already comply. The list is P11's work queue.

A bare <img> decodes on the main thread and fetches at full priority the moment
it is parsed, off-screen or not. On the mid-range Android this platform is
measured on, that is jank on a screen the member has not reached.

Accepts loading="lazy"|"eager" and decoding="async"|"sync"|"auto", or any
expression — the attribute is present and this rule does not evaluate it. A
literal that is not one of those values is reported: a typo reads as done. A
{...spread} is reported rather than assumed to supply them; unknown is not a
pass (C-34). Scope mirrors the inventory: shipped src/** only, not the UI
harness and not the test tree — verified, no allowlisted path is flagged.

⚠ RECORDED, NOT HIDDEN: the rule cannot see `<img` written inside an HTML
template string — 7 sites at 0-D2-03, inventory §2b. ESLint sees a string, not
a tag. Those are P11's second half and need their own check; a green run of
this rule is not a complete P11.

Wired at "error", so it is RED until P11's sweep lands. The repository's own
precedent for a baselined rule is "warn" first, flipped to "error" once src/ is
clean (no-raw-tailwind-colors); that one word is the Auditor's call, and either
way this must not land before, or apart from, the sweep it gates.

Six RuleTester invalid cases and eight valid ones prove the rule can fail
independently of src/ and stay meaningful after the sweep: bare tag, loading
without decoding, decoding without loading, two typo'd values, and a spread.

npx tsc -b tsconfig.json exit 0. `npm run lint` was already red before this
commit — 1,839 errors from other rules, a pre-existing baseline this unit does
not touch; the 119 above are this rule's own and are counted separately.

